  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RL Guinea - Morocco on Wastewater Treatment Plant Construction Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overarching objective of the Wastewater Treatment Development Project in Conakry, Guinea, is to achieve a sustainable improvement in the provision of sanitation services by treating collected wastewater before discharging it into the ocean, thus safeguarding public health and protecting the environment. Specifically, the project aims to:

1. Upgrade and Expand WWTP Capacity: Enhance and expand the capacity of the existing wastewater treatment plant to 25,800 m&#xb3;/day by 2027, ensuring treated wastewater meets international standards.

2. Improve Institutional and Regulatory Framework: Strengthen the governance of the sanitation sector by updating and reforming the institutional and regulatory frameworks to facilitate efficient management and sustainable operations.

3. Develop Local Capacity: Train 144 staff members from the Executing Agency and other stakeholders in the sanitation sector by 2027, ensuring they possess the necessary skills for effective management and maintenance of the sanitation infrastructure.

4. Ensure Project Sustainability: Assist the Executing Agency in operating and maintaining the WWTP during the first two years post-completion to guarantee the longevity and efficacy of the project&#x2019;s outcomes.

